<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tuman bay II</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1517">1517</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Al-Ashraf Tuman bay</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tuman bay II was the last sultan of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mamluk-sultanate">Mamluk Sultanate</a>, chosen in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cairo">Cairo</a> in 1516 after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qansuh-al-ghawri">Qansuh al-Ghawri</a> was killed at Marj Dabiq. He resisted the Ottoman invasion but was defeated at Ridaniya in January 1517 and fought on in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guerrilla-warfare">guerrilla</a> actions. Betrayed by a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bedouin">Bedouin</a> chief, he was captured and hanged at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bab-zuwayla">Bab Zuwayla</a> gate in Cairo in April 1517.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tuman-bay-ii.jpg" alt="Tuman bay II" width="320" height="419" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Paolo Giovio · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tumanbay_II_(81651932).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
